sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant A as Agent (workload identity)
    participant STS as Enterprise STS (ICAM)
    participant G as Grant Store (ICAM)
    participant EG as Enterprise MCP Gateway
    participant DG as Domain MCP Gateway (Cerbos)
    participant M as MCP Server

    rect rgb(235, 242, 250)
    Note over U,G: One-time setup for async use (user signed in)
    U->>STS: Authenticate (step-up for broad scopes)
    U->>G: Create delegation grant (agent-x, scope, expiry)
    G-->>U: grant_id g-123
    end

    alt User present (interactive)
        U->>A: Request + live user token
        A->>STS: OBO exchange (subject = user token, actor = agent credential)
    else User absent (async)
        A->>STS: Token exchange (actor = agent credential, grant_id g-123)
        STS->>G: Validate grant and revocation status
    end
    STS->>STS: Re-check user's current attributes and recent-login rule
    STS-->>A: T1: sub=adam, act=agent-x, aud=enterprise-gw, exp 5m, bound to agent key

    A->>EG: Tool call + T1 (DPoP proof)
    EG->>EG: Validate signature, aud, binding, act present. Coarse policy and tool registry
    EG->>STS: Exchange T1 (actor = EG credential, resource = domain-gw, narrower scope)
    STS-->>EG: T2: sub=adam, act=agent-x, aud=domain-gw, narrower scope, exp not beyond T1
    EG->>DG: Tool call + T2
    DG->>DG: Cerbos ABAC (principal = adam attrs, actor = agent-x, resource attrs)
    DG->>STS: Exchange T2 (resource = mcp-server, single tool)
    STS-->>DG: T3: sub=adam, act=agent-x, aud=mcp-server, exp seconds to minutes
    DG->>M: Invoke tool + T3
    M-->>DG: Result
    DG-->>EG: Result
    EG-->>A: Result

    Note over STS,G: CAEP/SSF event (offboarding, attribute change) revokes grant. Next exchange fails.
